From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: arm64: dts: h713: add the HY320 board dts

The MagCubic HY320 (stock Android 11 userland on the ADT-3 vendor build
6245789, kernel 5.4.99, vendor U-Boot and ARISC of 2024-04-19) has the
HY350's DRAM words and display firmware ("ADT-3 2024", 1252128 bytes) and
a 1080p dual-port panel at project 0x30. Its tree is the HY310's, held
against this board's own stock device trees (vendor_boot_a and the sunxi
package of the owner's eMMC dump), with the HY300 Pro's choices where the
stock tree is ambiguous - the same vendor family, and the board has no
serial console:

- The lamp: the display firmware's PWM 5 words from this board's
  panel_config.ini [PWMSetting] (channel 5, polarity 1, 40 kHz, vsync
  lock 1, duty 1..100), as on the HY300 Pro (0166a), no pin group.
  pwm-backlight off: the stock tree disables pwm2 (PB4) and pwm3 (PB5)
  and names PB5 only as tvtop panel_bl_en, a plain GPIO.
- The fan: the stock "fan" node claims PH17 as PWM0's pin and as
  fan1-fg-gpio, U-Boot's fan_ctrl names it once more - the HY310's and
  the HY300 Pro's pattern, where PH17 is the tacho (measured on the
  HY310, counted on the HY300 Pro). So the dtsi's fan0 stays: tacho PH17,
  no PWM. PB5 stays the dtsi's hog, as on the HY300 Pro.
- No NTC evaluation: the stock node reads one on GPADC channel 1, with
  tables of another driver whose units are not known here; ntc_num stays
  0 and no power-off hangs on an unproven conversion.
- The focus motor off: the stock motor_ctr is disabled.
- The accelerometer node off: the chip at 0x18 on twi1 is an STK8BA58
  (stock "stk,stk83xx"), not the HY310's SC7A20, and no driver here is
  shown to fit it.
- The display firmware's elog addresses: ring 0x8b271d9c and write cell
  0x8b48b2a8 of U-Boot's "ADT-3 2024" row, the control block 0x4a8 below
  the write cell as on the HY310 and the HY300 Pro: <0x4b48ae00
  0x4b271d9c> in ARM view.
- The vendor ARISC firmware and no display MIPS restart, as on the
  HY300 Pro.

Power key PL4 and IR on PL9 are the HY310's by the stock tree, and its IR
address list holds the 0xfd02 and 0xff00 remotes rc-h713-fd02 maps.

Built (dtc, against the series applied to 6.18.38); not booted. The image
built from it is a TEST image for the board's owner.

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy310.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-l018.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy320.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-h728-x96qpro+.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-t527-avaota-a1.dtb
diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy320.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy320.dts
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy320.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,163 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+/*
+ * MagCubic HY320 projector (stock Android 11 userland on the ADT-3 vendor
+ * build 6245789, kernel 5.4.99; vendor U-Boot and ARISC of 2024-04-19).
+ *
+ * The HY310's tree, held against this board's own stock device trees (the
+ * kernel's in vendor_boot_a and U-Boot's in the sunxi package, read off the
+ * owner's eMMC dump). The panel is project 0x30, 1920x1080 dual port, as on
+ * the HY310 and the HY350; the display firmware is the "ADT-3 2024"
+ * revision (1252128 bytes, the HY350's and the HY300 T08's), not the
+ * HY310's. Nothing on this board has been measured by us and there is no
+ * serial console on it: where its stock tree is silent or ambiguous, this
+ * file keeps what the HY300 Pro, the nearest board of the same vendor
+ * family, runs with. What differs, and what this file does about it:
+ *
+ *  - The lamp: panel_config.ini [PWMSetting] says hardware channel 5,
+ *    polarity 1, 40 kHz, vsync lock 1, duty 1..100 - the HY300 Pro's six
+ *    words, handed to the display firmware. PB4 (pwm2) and PB5 (pwm3) carry
+ *    no PWM under stock (both nodes disabled; PB5 is tvtop panel_bl_en as a
+ *    plain GPIO), so pwm-backlight is off.
+ *  - The fan: the stock "fan" node claims PH17 twice, as PWM0's pin and as
+ *    fan1-fg-gpio, and U-Boot's fan_ctrl names PH17 again - the pattern the
+ *    HY310's and the HY300 Pro's stock trees have, where PH17 is the tacho
+ *    (measured on the HY310; counted on the HY300 Pro). So the dtsi's fan0
+ *    stays: tacho PH17, no PWM, the fan on PB5. PB5 stays the dtsi's hog,
+ *    as on the HY300 Pro.
+ *  - No NTC evaluation: the stock fan node reads one (temp_det_source 1,
+ *    GPADC channel 1 by its gpadc node's channel_select), but with tables
+ *    of another driver whose conversion is not known here.
+ *  - The focus motor is disabled under stock: off here.
+ *  - The accelerometer at 0x18 on twi1 is an STK8BA58 (stk,stk83xx), not
+ *    the HY310's SC7A20: its node is off here.
+ *  - The display firmware's elog addresses, the vendor ARISC image, and no
+ *    display MIPS restart (measured on the HY310 only).
+ *
+ * The same as the HY310 by its stock tree: power key PL4 (standby_param,
+ * keyboard power-gpio), IR on PL9 (cir_param; its address list holds the
+ * 0xfd02 and 0xff00 remotes the dtsi's rc-h713-fd02 maps).
+ */
+
+#include "sun50i-h713-hy310.dts"
+
+/ {
+	model = "MagCubic HY320";
+	compatible = "magcubic,hy320", "allwinner,sun50i-h713";
+};
+
+/*
+ * Nothing on this board is driven by the dtsi's pwm-backlight (PWM2/PB4):
+ * the stock tree disables pwm2@2000c12 (PB4) and pwm3@2000c13 (PB5) and
+ * names PB5 only as tvtop panel_bl_en, a plain GPIO high - the HY300 Pro's
+ * state (0161a). A live /sys/class/backlight is what systemd-backlight
+ * writes to at boot; there is none here.
+ */
+&backlight {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+/* The vendor ARISC image, as on the HY300 Pro: crust has run on the HY310 only. */
+&arisc {
+	firmware-name = "h713-arisc.bin", "hy310-edid.bin";
+};
+
+/* The display MIPS restart is measured on the HY310 only. */
+&mips {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+/*
+ * PB5 enables the LED boost and the fan rail (stock tvtop panel_bl_en, a
+ * GPIO): the dtsi's hog holds it high, not the board manager - as on the
+ * HY300 Pro, so nothing in Linux ever drives it low.
+ */
+&fan_power_hog {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+/*
+ * The fan. The stock kernel's "fan" node (pwm-fan, the vendor's driver)
+ * names pwms = PWM0, whose stock pin group pwm0@0 is PH17, and
+ * fan1-fg-gpio = PH17 as well; U-Boot's tree enables fan_ctrl with
+ * fanctrl-gpios = PH17. The HY310's stock node claimed PH17 the same two
+ * ways and PH17 is its tacho (the dtsi's board manager comment); on the
+ * HY300 Pro, of this board's vendor family, our tacho counted on PH17
+ * (boards/hy300-pro). So fan0 keeps the dtsi's tacho on PH17 and no PWM:
+ * a PWM0 output on PH17 would drive against the tacho line. The board
+ * manager powers off when the tacho counts below 1000 RPM for 8 s, so this
+ * pin decides whether the board stays up.
+ *
+ * No temperature: the stock node evaluates an NTC (temp_det_enable 1,
+ * temp_det_source 1 = GPADC; the gpadc node's channel_select 0x02 is
+ * channel 1) with its own tables (gpadc-temp 0..90 C against gpadc-adc
+ * 0x553..0xcc) and fan speeds above 60/68/72/76 C, no power-off. Those
+ * tables belong to another driver, and whether their numbers are mV, as
+ * this driver's gpadc-table is, or raw counts is not known here; the
+ * L018's table is not this board's. So ntc_num stays the HY310's 0, and
+ * nothing hangs a power-off on an unproven conversion.
+ */
+&board_mgr {
+	fan0 {
+		/delete-property/ fan-power-gpio;
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * This board's display firmware ("ADT-3 2024", U-Boot's h713_mips_fw_revs[]
+ * row) keeps its event log 0x1000 below the HY310's: mode-1 ring
+ * 0x8b271d9c and write cell 0x8b48b2a8 in MIPS view. The control block is
+ * the write cell less 0x4a8, as on the HY310 (0x8b48c2a8 -> 0x4b48be00)
+ * and the HY300 Pro (0x8b48b6a8 -> 0x4b48b200, 0161b): 0x4b48ae00 in ARM
+ * view. Read on the unit (31.10.2026): cpu_comm's dump at boot shows the
+ * firmware's own lines (HdmiRx_HDCP14_LoadKey time-outs).
+ */
+&cpu_comm {
+	allwinner,elog = <0x4b48ae00 0x4b271d9c>;
+};
+
+/*
+ * The display state this board's boot loader hands over. Our U-Boot ran the
+ * whole display init on the unit (31.10.2026, its console recorded to the
+ * eMMC: "boot logo up ... with the firmware running", the logo seen on the
+ * wall), and the AFBD then read CTRL 0x03001901 - the HY310's - but
+ * VIDEO_CTRL 0x03000200 and an LVDS selector of 0 where the HY310's
+ * firmware leaves 0x03000010 and 0x29000000. The "ADT-3 2024" firmware
+ * leaves the video channel and the selector as it does; with the HY310's
+ * defaults the driver refused to probe and the wall went black after the
+ * logo. These are the words this board's handoff consists of, and the ones
+ * the driver puts back when the video plane goes away.
+ */
+&display {
+	allwinner,handoff-state = <0x03001901 0x03000200 0x00000000>;
+};
+
+/*
+ * The lamp's dimmer is a PWM the display firmware owns. This board's
+ * panel_config.ini [PWMSetting]: pwm_channel 5, polarity 1 (low active),
+ * 40000 Hz, vs_lock 1, min 1, max 100 - the HY300 Pro's words (0166a),
+ * which the vendor's PanelControl hands to the firmware at start. No pin
+ * group: the stock pwm5@2000c15 node names no pins (0166a).
+ */
+&hdmirx {
+	allwinner,backlight-pwm-info = <5 1 40000 1 1 100>;
+};
+
+/*
+ * The stock motor_ctr is status "disabled" (pins PH4..PH7, limiter PH14,
+ * as on the HY310), so the driver neither homes nor drives a motor here.
+ */
+&motor_ctr {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+/*
+ * twi1 stays on as under stock (PH2/PH3, 100 kHz). Its chip at 0x18 is an
+ * STK8BA58 (stock "stk,stk83xx", irq PB0); mainline's stk8ba50 driver is
+ * for the STK8BA50, and nothing here shows the two share a register map,
+ * so the dtsi's SC7A20 node is off rather than bound to the wrong chip.
+ */
+&twi1 {
+	accelerometer@18 {
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+};
